From: =?UTF-8?q?S=C3=A9bastien=20Celles?= <s.celles@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 7 Jun 2026 09:56:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 39/62] verimark: skip 0x96 03 commit on the IT (firmware
 auto-commits via 0x8006)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

After the previous patch, the IT enroll proceeded through the
'add_image returns 0x8006' interpretation and jumped to
ENR_S_COMMIT_CALL, where 0x96 03 was rejected with status 0x0404
(VERIMARK_STATUS_BAD_STATE). The IT firmware is already in idle
state at that point — the 0x8006 itself was the commit.

Patch ENR_S_COMMIT_CALL : when the device is the IT, log and
fpi_ssm_next_state directly to ENR_S_DB_REFRESH without sending
0x96 03. The downstream DB_REFRESH / FINISH / GETLIST_POST /
RESOLVE_TUID chain still runs, so the new TUID is still found via
the pre/post getlist diff exactly like on the DT.

The DT path is unchanged when PID == 0x00F2.
---
 libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c b/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
index 38a7846..cbf75d7 100644
--- a/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
+++ b/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
@@ -2531,6 +2531,18 @@ enroll_sm_run_state(FpiSsm *ssm, FpDevice *dev)
         fpi_ssm_next_state(ssm);
         return;
     case ENR_S_COMMIT_CALL: {
+        /* IT firmware auto-commits when it signals enroll-complete via
+         * 0x8006 on add_image. Sending the DT-style 0x96 03 commit on
+         * the IT is rejected with VERIMARK_STATUS_BAD_STATE (0x0404)
+         * because the firmware is already in idle state. Skip to
+         * DB_REFRESH so the new TUID is still resolved via the pre/post
+         * getlist diff (same as the DT post-commit path). */
+        GUsbDevice *usb = fpi_device_get_usb_device(dev);
+        if (usb != NULL && g_usb_device_get_pid(usb) == VERIMARK_PID_IT) {
+            fp_info("verimark: IT enroll skipping 0x96 03 (firmware auto-commits)");
+            fpi_ssm_next_state(ssm);
+            return;
+        }
         uint8_t commit_payload[123];
         enr_build_commit_payload(ctx->new_tuid, commit_payload);
         verimark_session_call_opcode_async(&self->session, self->transport,
